            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-nxp/meta-imx93/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There's a lot of stuff here that shouldn't be done through IMAGE_INSTALL directive like this.  The problem is that if someone wants to build a separate initramfs from a rootfs, you are now shoving all these applications into the initramfs.\n\nIf you want to modify obmc-phosphor-image, do it with a obmc-phosphor-image.bbappend, but I suspect many of these things here aren't even appropriate to put there.  phosphor-hwmon, dbus-sensors, entity-manager are all supposed to be driven by openbmc features.  lmsensors isn't supported by OpenBMC; neither is openipmi."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-nxp/meta-imx93/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "??  You are running git on the BMC itself?"
